  "description": "Overview On the Occasion of IBM + Qiskit Fall Fest Welcome to QuHack 2026 , an online hackathon focused on Quantum Computing, Quantum Machine Learning, and emerging technologies . Participants will compete in teams to solve one of 100 unique problem statements and build innovative solutions using quantum computing concepts and technologies. What to Expect? 100 problem statements to choose from Team-based participation Quantum Computing and Qiskit-focused challenges Opportunity to build and develop your solution Solution and presentation submission Evaluation by judges Prizes and recognition Hackathon Process Register Register individually or as a team. Choose a Challenge Choose one of the 100 problem statements released for the hackathon. Build Work with your team to develop your solution. Submit Submit your solution along with the required PPT/documentation before the deadline. Evaluation Submissions will be evaluated based on innovation, technical implementation, problem-solving approach, and relevance to the problem statement. Results The best solutions will be selected as the winners of QuHack 2026. Recommended Skills Quantum Computing Qiskit Machine Learning Programming Problem Solving No prior professional experience is required. Participants are encouraged to learn, experiment, and build during the hackathon. Prizes & Recognition Cash prizes of up to ₹2,00,000 Certificates and recognition for winning teams and outstanding participants Special recognition and opportunities from participating industry sponsors may also be available Who Can Participate? The hackathon is open to students, developers, researchers, and technology enthusiasts interested in exploring quantum computing. 100 Challenges. One Hackathon. Your Solution. Register for QuHack 2026 and start building!",
