    "details": "<p><strong>Overview</strong></p>\n<p>On the Occasion of IBM + Qiskit Fall Fest</p>\n<p>Welcome to <strong>QuHack 2026</strong>, an online hackathon focused on <strong>Quantum Computing, Quantum Machine Learning, and emerging technologies</strong>.</p>\n<p>Participants will compete in teams to solve one of <strong>100 unique problem statements</strong> and build innovative solutions using quantum computing concepts and technologies.</p>\n<p><strong>What to Expect?</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>100 problem statements to choose from</li>\n<li>Team-based participation</li>\n<li>Quantum Computing and Qiskit-focused challenges</li>\n<li>Opportunity to build and develop your solution</li>\n<li>Solution and presentation submission</li>\n<li>Evaluation by judges</li>\n<li>Prizes and recognition</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Hackathon Process</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Register</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Register individually or as a team.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Choose a Challenge</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Choose <strong>one of the 100 problem statements</strong> released for the hackathon.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Build</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Work with your team to develop your solution.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Submit</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Submit your solution along with the required PPT/documentation before the deadline.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Evaluation</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Submissions will be evaluated based on innovation, technical implementation, problem-solving approach, and relevance to the problem statement.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Results</strong></p>\n<p>The best solutions will be selected as the winners of QuHack 2026.</p>\n<p><strong>Recommended Skills</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Quantum Computing</li>\n<li>Qiskit</li>\n<li>Machine Learning</li>\n<li>Programming</li>\n<li>Problem Solving</li>\n</ul>\n<p>No prior professional experience is required. Participants are encouraged to learn, experiment, and build during the hackathon.</p>\n<p><strong>Prizes &amp; Recognition</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Cash prizes of up to ₹2,00,000</li>\n<li>Certificates and recognition for winning teams and outstanding participants</li>\n<li>Special recognition and opportunities from participating industry sponsors may also be available</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Who Can Participate?</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The hackathon is open to <strong>students, developers, researchers, and technology enthusiasts</strong> interested in exploring quantum computing.</li>\n<li>100 Challenges. One Hackathon. Your Solution.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Register for QuHack 2026 and start building!</strong></p>",
